from __future__ import annotations

"""
Run a read-only extraction audit on 4 dermatology articles that are intentionally
kept away from prompt few-shot / previously targeted topics.

Why this script exists:
- The earlier targeted audit used articles that later became prompt examples.
- This script chooses 4 different articles and reports extraction quality without
  hard-coding expected endpoint terms from the prompt.

Safety:
- No Neo4j writes.
- No Qdrant writes.
- No ingest/build step.
- No --fresh/delete-output behavior.
- Existing files in --out-dir may be overwritten, but the directory is not deleted.

Outputs:
- unbiased_extraction_audit.md: readable audit + manual review sections
- unbiased_extraction_summary.csv: one row per selected article
- unbiased_relations.csv: flattened validated relations
- unbiased_entities.csv: flattened validated entities
- unbiased_chunks.csv: one row per extraction window/chunk
